  "Question": "Use 36 m of fencing to enclose a rectangular livestock pen, with a fence through the middle parallel to the width dividing it into two smaller rectangles (the total fence length includes the partition). Find the maximum area of the pen. (Unit: \\(\\mathrm{m}^2\\))",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "54",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Let the width be \\(x\\ \\mathrm{m}\\). The fencing includes two lengths and three widths, so the length is \\((36-3x)/2\\ \\mathrm{m}\\), with \\(0<x<12\\). Thus the area is\n\\[\nS=x(36-3x)/2=-1.5(x-6)^2+54.\n\\]\nSince \\((x-6)^2\\ge0\\), the maximum area is \\(54\\ \\mathrm{m}^2\\), attained when \\(x=6\\) and the length is \\(9\\ \\mathrm{m}\\).",
